commit b12b2244
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 12:18:51 -0600
subject: fix(streaming): prevent duplicate [DONE] sentinel in passthrough mode

BUG: All passthrough streaming (single-model AND combo) sent `data: [DONE]`
twice to the client, violating the OpenAI SSE protocol.

ROOT CAUSE: In open-sse/utils/stream.js, the passthrough transform() path
forwards the upstream [DONE] line via the generic forwarder but never sets
`streamDoneSent = true`. The flush() handler then adds a second [DONE]
because its guard `!streamDoneSent` passes.

The streamDoneSent tracking was implemented for translate mode (where
[DONE] is detected via parsed.done) but was never extended to passthrough
mode when it was added. This is an internal implementation gap — no
external PR or contribution introduced it.

FIX (2 files):
1. open-sse/utils/stream.js: Added `if (trimmed === "data: [DONE]")
   streamDoneSent = true;` after the passthrough forwarder enqueues output.
   This marks the sentinel as sent so flush() skips the duplicate.

2. open-sse/handlers/chatCore.js: Extended the forced-SSE-to-JSON guard
   to also trigger when `stream` is true (upstream defaulted to streaming)
   even if providerRequiresStreaming is false. This ensures non-streaming
   clients never receive raw SSE when the upstream forces streaming.
   Comment updated to explain the dual condition.

VERIFICATION (production standalone build, port 20130, mock upstream 24000):
- Single-model streaming: 2x [DONE] → 1x [DONE] ✓
- Combo streaming: 2x [DONE] → 1x [DONE] ✓
- Non-streaming combo: clean JSON ✓
- Direct mock upstream: 1x [DONE] (unchanged) ✓

FOUND BY: GitHub Copilot agent during E2E testing with mock upstream.
NOT from any external PR or user-reported issue.

LEARNING: learnings/2026-08-06-sse-done-duplicate-leak.md (local only,
docs/plans-and-prompts is gitignored)
ADR: decisions/ADR-005-sse-done-tracking-passthrough.md (local only)

Part of: Smart Router & Fallback UX plan (M4 polish)


